{
  "id": "cd3e25a3-6ba6-48a8-baba-346ea9780315",
  "productId": "openmrs",
  "title": "Impact of ConceptService.saveDrug Change",
  "updatedAt": 1793548592219,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "ODp1njRshq2TUuiM",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "If the behaviour of `ConceptService.saveDrug` in openmrs-core changed, which code in the REST web services module (openmrs-module-webservices.rest) uses it and could be affected?",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "grounded",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Changing `ConceptService.saveDrug` in openmrs-core would affect the REST web services module in three production resources plus one test class. In openmrs-core the method is declared on the API interface `ConceptService.saveDrug` [1], declared again on the DAO [2], and implemented in `ConceptServiceImpl.saveDrug`, which simply checks whether the service is locked and delegates to the DAO [3]. The actual persistence work lives in `HibernateConceptDAO.saveDrug` [4].",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I searched the whole openmrs-module-webservices.rest repository for the symbol `saveDrug`, so the list below is complete for that module.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Confirmed call sites",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "| Location | How it calls `saveDrug` | What a behaviour change would touch |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DrugResource1_8.save` [5] | `Context.getConceptService().saveDrug(delegate)` and returns the result | The `/drug` REST endpoint, and every create/update of a drug via REST |\n| `DrugReferenceMapResource1_10.save` [6] | Adds the map to the parent drug, then saves the drug | The `/drugreferencemap` endpoint; the map itself is persisted only as a side effect of saving the drug |\n| `DrugIngredientResource1_11.save` [7] | Adds the ingredient to the parent drug when missing, then saves the drug | The nested `/drug/{uuid}/ingredient` endpoint |\n| `DrugIngredientResource1_11.purge` [8] | Removes the ingredient from the drug, nulls its drug, then saves the drug | Deleting an ingredient through REST |\n| `DrugController1_10Test` [9] | Sets `strength`, saves, then reads the drug back through the controller | Two tests, `shouldIncludeStrengthInDefaultRepresentation` and `shouldIncludeStrengthInFullRepresentation`; they would fail if saving stopped persisting `strength` |",
          "citations": [
            5,
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Why the reach is wider than `DrugResource1_8`",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The `save` override sits on `DrugResource1_8` [10], which is the base class for the newer drug resources: `DrugResource1_10` extends it [11], `DrugResource1_11` extends `DrugResource1_10` [12], and `DrugResource1_12` extends `DrugResource1_11` [13]. None of them overrides `save`, so on OpenMRS 1.12 and above (the `1.12.* - 9.*` range on `DrugResource1_12`) the active `/drug` resource still inherits the `saveDrug` call. `DrugResource1_11` also routes the `ingredients` property through a `@PropertySetter` [14] and exposes `ingredients` as a sub-resource [15], which is what makes `DrugIngredientResource1_11` reachable.",
          "citations": [
            10,
            11,
            12,
            13,
            14,
            15
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "```archify\n{\"schema_version\":1,\"diagram_type\":\"architecture\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Who reaches ConceptService.saveDrug from webservices.rest\"},\"components\":[{\"id\":\"api\",\"type\":\"external\",\"label\":\"REST clients\",\"sublabel\":\"/drug, ingredient, drugreferencemap\",\"row\":0,\"col\":0},{\"id\":\"drug18\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugResource1_8\",\"sublabel\":\"save() calls saveDrug\",\"row\":1,\"col\":1},{\"id\":\"drug110\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugResource1_10\",\"sublabel\":\"extends 1_8\",\"row\":0,\"col\":2},{\"id\":\"drug111\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugResource1_11\",\"sublabel\":\"extends 1_10\",\"row\":1,\"col\":2},{\"id\":\"drug112\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugResource1_12\",\"sublabel\":\"extends 1_11\",\"row\":2,\"col\":2},{\"id\":\"ingredient\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugIngredientResource1_11\",\"sublabel\":\"save and purge call saveDrug\",\"row\":2,\"col\":0},{\"id\":\"refmap\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"DrugReferenceMapResource1_10\",\"sublabel\":\"save calls saveDrug\",\"row\":3,\"col\":0},{\"id\":\"svc\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"ConceptServiceImpl.saveDrug\",\"sublabel\":\"the changed method\",\"row\":3,\"col\":3},{\"id\":\"dao\",\"type\":\"database\",\"label\":\"HibernateConceptDAO.saveDrug\",\"row\":4,\"col\":3}],\"connections\":[{\"from\":\"api\",\"to\":\"drug18\",\"label\":\"CREATE or UPDATE drug\"},{\"from\":\"drug110\",\"to\":\"drug18\",\"label\":\"inherits save\"},{\"from\":\"drug111\",\"to\":\"drug110\",\"label\":\"inherits save\"},{\"from\":\"drug112\",\"to\":\"drug111\",\"label\":\"inherits save\"},{\"from\":\"api\",\"to\":\"ingredient\",\"label\":\"nested ingredient\"},{\"from\":\"api\",\"to\":\"refmap\",\"label\":\"drug reference map\"},{\"from\":\"drug18\",\"to\":\"svc\",\"label\":\"calls\"},{\"from\":\"ingredient\",\"to\":\"svc\",\"label\":\"calls\"},{\"from\":\"refmap\",\"to\":\"svc\",\"label\":\"calls\"},{\"from\":\"svc\",\"to\":\"dao\",\"label\":\"delegates\"}]}\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## What I could not check",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "I only searched openmrs-module-webservices.rest, and only for the literal name `saveDrug`. A behaviour change could also surface through reflection, Spring/Hibernate configuration, or through other modules or frontend clients (for example the O3 patient chart or dispensing app) that consume the `/drug`, `/drug/{uuid}/ingredient` and `/drugreferencemap` endpoints. Those are outside the scope of this question and were not read.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
